IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa-definitions`
IMPORT `coa1-part3-constitution`

-- coa1-tests-part3.l4: tests for coa1-part3-constitution.l4 (ss 17 to 38 of the Companies Act 2006).
-- Every expected value was decided by reading the section's words (quoted beside each group) before the run, and is written beside
-- the assertion; none was copied from the module's own output. Arguments follow the GIVEN order of each rule.
-- Dates and pound amounts are illustrative test inputs, not figures from the Act (the Act's own figures, 15 and 28 days, 0.1 of level 3,
-- GBP 200, are in the rules). A DEONTIC value cannot be compared in an #ASSERT on the stable binary, so each #TRACE states its expected
-- outcome in a comment and is read, not asserted.

`s 32(1) test profile limited by shares with a share capital` MEANS `Company profile` WITH
    `place of registration` IS `England and Wales`
    `liability of the members` IS `liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held`
    `a share capital` IS TRUE
    `certificate of incorporation stating that it is a public company` IS FALSE
`s 32(1) test profile limited by guarantee without a share capital` MEANS `Company profile` WITH
    `place of registration` IS `Scotland`
    `liability of the members` IS `liability limited to the amount the members undertake to contribute on a winding up`
    `a share capital` IS FALSE
    `certificate of incorporation stating that it is a public company` IS FALSE
`s 32(1) test profile limited by guarantee with a share capital` MEANS `Company profile` WITH
    `place of registration` IS `Northern Ireland`
    `liability of the members` IS `liability limited to the amount the members undertake to contribute on a winding up`
    `a share capital` IS TRUE
    `certificate of incorporation stating that it is a public company` IS FALSE
`s 32(1) test profile unlimited` MEANS `Company profile` WITH
    `place of registration` IS `England and Wales`
    `liability of the members` IS `liability not limited`
    `a share capital` IS FALSE
    `certificate of incorporation stating that it is a public company` IS FALSE

-- ---- s 17 ----
-- "references in the Companies Acts to a company's constitution include— (a) the company's articles, and (b) any resolutions and agreements to which Chapter 3 applies"
#ASSERT `s 17 the document is part of the company's constitution` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 17 the document is part of the company's constitution` FALSE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 17 the document is part of the company's constitution` FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 17 the document is part of the company's constitution` FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 17 the document is part of the company's constitution` FALSE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 18 ----
-- "(1) A company must have articles of association prescribing regulations for the company."
#ASSERT `s 18(1) the company has articles of association as required` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 18(1) the company has articles of association as required` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "(2) Unless it is a company to which model articles apply by virtue of section 20 (default application of model articles in case of limited company), it must register articles of association."
#ASSERT `s 18(2) the company must register articles of association` `liability not limited` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 18(2) the company must register articles of association` `liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 18(2) the company must register articles of association` `liability limited to the amount the members undertake to contribute on a winding up` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the duty, run (read, not asserted). Expected, in order: FULFILLED (an unlimited company registers); the standing obligation (an unlimited company has not registered, no time limit in the text); FULFILLED (a limited company has no duty to register).
#TRACE `s 18(2) the company's duty to register articles` `liability not limited` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `s 18(2) register articles of association with the registrar` AT 5
#TRACE `s 18(2) the company's duty to register articles` `liability not limited` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 100)
#TRACE `s 18(2) the company's duty to register articles` `liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 100)
-- "(3) Articles of association registered by a company must— (a) be contained in a single document, and (b) be divided into paragraphs numbered consecutively."
#ASSERT `s 18(3) the registered articles meet the requirements as to form` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 18(3) the registered articles meet the requirements as to form` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 18(3) the registered articles meet the requirements as to form` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "(4) References in the Companies Acts to a company's “articles” are to its articles of association."
#ASSERT `s 18(4) the reference in the Companies Acts is to the company's articles of association` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 18(4) the reference in the Companies Acts is to the company's articles of association` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---- s 19 ----
-- "(3) A company may adopt all or any of the provisions of model articles."
#ASSERT `s 19(3) the company may adopt the provisions of model articles` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 19(3) the company may adopt the provisions of model articles` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "(4) Any amendment of model articles by regulations under this section does not affect a company registered before the amendment takes effect. “Amendment” here includes addition, alteration or repeal."
#ASSERT `s 19(4) an amendment of the model articles affects the company` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 19(4) an amendment of the model articles affects the company` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 19(4) the change to the model articles is an amendment` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 19(4) the change to the model articles is an amendment` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 19(4) the change to the model articles is an amendment` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 19(4) the change to the model articles is an amendment` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 20 ----
-- "(1) On the formation of a limited company— (a) if articles are not registered, or (b) if articles are registered, in so far as they do not exclude or modify the relevant model articles, the relevant model articles (so far as applicable) form part of the company's articles"
#ASSERT `s 20(1) the provision of the relevant model articles forms part of the company's articles` `liability not limited` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 20(1) the provision of the relevant model articles forms part of the company's articles` `liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 20(1) the provision of the relevant model articles forms part of the company's articles` `liability limited to the amount the members undertake to contribute on a winding up` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 20(1) the provision of the relevant model articles forms part of the company's articles` `liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 20(1) the provision of the relevant model articles forms part of the company's articles` `liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 20(1) the provision of the relevant model articles forms part of the company's articles` `liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "(2) The “relevant model articles” means the model articles prescribed for a company of that description as in force at the date on which the company is registered."
`s 20(2) test version A` MEANS `s 20(2) version of the model articles` OF (Date 1 10 2009), "A"
`s 20(2) test version B` MEANS `s 20(2) version of the model articles` OF (Date 1 5 2013), "B"
#ASSERT `s 20(2) the relevant model articles` (Date 1 6 2010) (LIST `s 20(2) test version A`, `s 20(2) test version B`) EQUALS JUST "A"
#ASSERT `s 20(2) the relevant model articles` (Date 30 4 2013) (LIST `s 20(2) test version A`, `s 20(2) test version B`) EQUALS JUST "A"
#ASSERT `s 20(2) the relevant model articles` (Date 1 5 2013) (LIST `s 20(2) test version A`, `s 20(2) test version B`) EQUALS JUST "B"
#ASSERT `s 20(2) the relevant model articles` (Date 1 6 2014) (LIST `s 20(2) test version B`, `s 20(2) test version A`) EQUALS JUST "B"
#ASSERT `s 20(2) the relevant model articles` (Date 30 9 2009) (LIST `s 20(2) test version A`, `s 20(2) test version B`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 20(2) the relevant model articles` (Date 1 6 2014) EMPTY EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 21 ----
-- "(1) A company may amend its articles by special resolution."
#ASSERT `s 21(1) the company may amend its articles by the resolution` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 21(1) the company may amend its articles by the resolution` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 21(1) the company may amend its articles by the resolution` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- "(2) In the case of a company that is a charity, this is subject to— (a) in England and Wales, sections 197 and 198 of the Charities Act 2011; (b) in Northern Ireland, section 96 of the Charities Act (Northern Ireland) 2008. (3) In the case of a company that is registered in the Scottish Charity Register, this is subject to— (a) section 112 of the Companies Act 1989 ..., and (b) section 16 of the Charities and Trustee Investment (Scotland) Act 2005"
#ASSERT `s 21(2) and (3) the enactments the power to amend articles is subject to` TRUE FALSE `England and Wales` EQUALS LIST `s 21 sections 197 and 198 of the Charities Act 2011`
#ASSERT `s 21(2) and (3) the enactments the power to amend articles is subject to` TRUE FALSE `Northern Ireland` EQUALS LIST `s 21 section 96 of the Charities Act (Northern Ireland) 2008`
#ASSERT `s 21(2) and (3) the enactments the power to amend articles is subject to` TRUE FALSE `Scotland` EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `s 21(2) and (3) the enactments the power to amend articles is subject to` FALSE FALSE `England and Wales` EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `s 21(2) and (3) the enactments the power to amend articles is subject to` FALSE TRUE `Scotland` EQUALS LIST `s 21 section 112 of the Companies Act 1989`, `s 21 section 16 of the Charities and Trustee Investment (Scotland) Act 2005`
#ASSERT `s 21(2) and (3) the enactments the power to amend articles is subject to` TRUE TRUE `England and Wales` EQUALS LIST `s 21 sections 197 and 198 of the Charities Act 2011`, `s 21 section 112 of the Companies Act 1989`, `s 21 section 16 of the Charities and Trustee Investment (Scotland) Act 2005`

-- ---- s 22 ----
-- "(1) A company's articles may contain provision (“provision for entrenchment”) to the effect that specified provisions of the articles may be amended or repealed only if conditions are met, or procedures are complied with, that are more restrictive than those applicable in the case of a special resolution."
#ASSERT `s 22(1) the provision is provision for entrenchment` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22(1) the provision is provision for entrenchment` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 22(1) the provision is provision for entrenchment` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "(2) Provision for entrenchment may only be made— (a) in the company's articles on formation, or (b) by an amendment of the company's articles agreed to by all the members of the company."
#ASSERT `s 22(2) provision for entrenchment may be made` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22(2) provision for entrenchment may be made` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22(2) provision for entrenchment may be made` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22(2) provision for entrenchment may be made` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "(3) Provision for entrenchment does not prevent amendment of the company's articles— (a) by agreement of all the members of the company, or (b) by order of a court or other authority having power to alter the company's articles."
#ASSERT `s 22(3) provision for entrenchment prevents the amendment` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 22(3) provision for entrenchment prevents the amendment` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 22(3) provision for entrenchment prevents the amendment` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "(4) Nothing in this section affects any power of a court or other authority to alter a company's articles."
#ASSERT `s 22(4) this section affects any power of a court or other authority to alter a company's articles` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---- s 23 ----
-- "(1) Where a company's articles— (a) on formation contain provision for entrenchment, (b) are amended so as to include such provision, or (c) are altered by order ... so as to restrict or exclude the power of the company to amend its articles, the company must give notice of that fact to the registrar."
#ASSERT `s 23(1) the company must give notice to the registrar of the entrenchment or restriction` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23(1) the company must give notice to the registrar of the entrenchment or restriction` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23(1) the company must give notice to the registrar of the entrenchment or restriction` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23(1) the company must give notice to the registrar of the entrenchment or restriction` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "(2) Where a company's articles— (a) are amended so as to remove provision for entrenchment, or (b) are altered by order— (i) so as to remove such provision, or (ii) so as to remove any other restriction on, or any exclusion of, the power of the company to amend its articles, the company must give notice of that fact to the registrar."
#ASSERT `s 23(2) the company must give notice to the registrar of the removal` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23(2) the company must give notice to the registrar of the removal` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23(2) the company must give notice to the registrar of the removal` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23(2) the company must give notice to the registrar of the removal` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the duties, run (read, not asserted). Expected, in order: FULFILLED; the standing obligation (no time limit in the text); FULFILLED (nothing triggers it); FULFILLED (removal notice given).
#TRACE `s 23(1) the company's duty to give notice of the restriction` TRUE FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `s 23(1) give the registrar notice that the articles contain, or are restricted by, provision for entrenchment` AT 4
#TRACE `s 23(1) the company's duty to give notice of the restriction` TRUE FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 100)
#TRACE `s 23(1) the company's duty to give notice of the restriction` FALSE FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 100)
#TRACE `s 23(2) the company's duty to give notice of the removal` TRUE FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `s 23(2) give the registrar notice that provision for entrenchment or another restriction has been removed` AT 4

-- ---- s 24 ----
-- "(1) This section applies where a company's articles are subject— (a) to provision for entrenchment, or (b) to an order of a court or other authority restricting or excluding the company's power to amend the articles."
#ASSERT `s 24(1) this section applies` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 24(1) this section applies` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 24(1) this section applies` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "(2) If the company— (a) amends its articles, and (b) is required to send to the registrar a document making or evidencing the amendment, the company must deliver with that document a statement of compliance."
#ASSERT `s 24(2) the company must deliver a statement of compliance with the document` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 24(2) the company must deliver a statement of compliance with the document` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 24(2) the company must deliver a statement of compliance with the document` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 24(2) the company must deliver a statement of compliance with the document` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 24(2) the company must deliver a statement of compliance with the document` NOTHING TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the duty, run (read, not asserted). Expected, in order: FULFILLED; the standing obligation (no time limit in the text); FULFILLED (the section does not apply).
#TRACE `s 24(2) the company's duty to deliver a statement of compliance` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `s 24(2) deliver a statement of compliance with the document` AT 2
#TRACE `s 24(2) the company's duty to deliver a statement of compliance` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 100)
#TRACE `s 24(2) the company's duty to deliver a statement of compliance` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 100)
-- "(3) The statement of compliance required is a statement certifying that the amendment has been made in accordance with the company's articles and, where relevant, any applicable order of a court or other authority."
#ASSERT `s 24(3) the statement is the statement of compliance required` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 24(3) the statement is the statement of compliance required` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 24(3) the statement is the statement of compliance required` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 24(3) the statement is the statement of compliance required` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "(4) The registrar may rely on the statement of compliance as sufficient evidence of the matters stated in it."
#ASSERT `s 24(4) the registrar may rely on the statement of compliance as sufficient evidence of the matters stated` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 24(4) the registrar may rely on the statement of compliance as sufficient evidence of the matters stated` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 24(4) the registrar may rely on the statement of compliance as sufficient evidence of the matters stated` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 25 ----
-- "(2) Subsection (1) does not apply in a case where the member agrees in writing, either before or after the alteration is made, to be bound by the alteration."
#ASSERT `s 25(2) subsection (1) applies to the member` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 25(2) subsection (1) applies to the member` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "(1) A member ... is not bound by an alteration to its articles after the date on which he became a member, if and so far as the alteration— (a) requires him to take or subscribe for more shares than the number held by him at the date on which the alteration is made, or (b) in any way increases his liability as at that date to contribute to the company's share capital or otherwise to pay money to the company."
#ASSERT `s 25(1) the member is not bound by the alteration` TRUE 11 10 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 25(1) the member is not bound by the alteration` TRUE 10 10 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 25(1) the member is not bound by the alteration` TRUE 9 10 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 25(1) the member is not bound by the alteration` TRUE 10 10 TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 25(1) the member is not bound by the alteration` FALSE 11 10 FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 25(1) the member is not bound by the alteration` TRUE 11 10 FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 25(1) the member is not bound by the alteration` TRUE 10 10 TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 26 ----
-- "(1) Where a company amends its articles it must send to the registrar a copy of the articles as amended not later than 15 days after the amendment takes effect." (amendment takes effect on 1 March 2026)
#ASSERT `s 26(1) the copy of the articles as amended was sent in time` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 16 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 26(1) the copy of the articles as amended was sent in time` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 17 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 26(1) the copy of the articles as amended was sent in time` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 26(1) the copy of the articles as amended was sent in time` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 28 2 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the duty, run (read, not asserted). Expected, in order: FULFILLED (day 15); BREACH (day 16); BREACH (nothing done by day 16).
#TRACE `s 26(1) the company's duty` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `s 26(1) send the registrar a copy of the articles as amended` AT 15
#TRACE `s 26(1) the company's duty` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `s 26(1) send the registrar a copy of the articles as amended` AT 16
#TRACE `s 26(1) the company's duty` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 16)
-- "(2) This section does not require a company to set out in its articles any provisions of model articles that— (a) are applied by the articles, or (b) apply by virtue of section 20"
#ASSERT `s 26(2) the company is required to set out the provision of model articles in its articles` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 26(2) the company is required to set out the provision of model articles in its articles` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 26(2) the company is required to set out the provision of model articles in its articles` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "(3) If a company fails to comply with this section an offence is committed by— (a) the company, and (b) every officer of the company who is in default."
#ASSERT `s 26(3)(a) the company commits an offence` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 26(3)(a) the company commits an offence` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 26(3)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 26(3)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 26(3)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 26(3)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "(4) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale."
#ASSERT `s 26(4) the penalty`'s `how convicted` EQUALS `on summary conviction`
#ASSERT `s 26(4) the penalty`'s `fine not exceeding` EQUALS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1)
#ASSERT `s 26(4) the penalty`'s `daily default fine for continued contravention` EQUALS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1)
#ASSERT `s 26(4) the penalty`'s `imprisonment not exceeding` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 26(4) the penalty`'s `imprisonment and fine together` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 26(4) the most the person can be fined on summary conviction, in pounds` 1000 EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT `s 26(4) the most the daily default fine can be for each day of continued contravention, in pounds` 1000 EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `s 26(4) the most the daily default fine can be for each day of continued contravention, in pounds` 1250 EQUALS 125

-- ---- s 27 ----
-- "(1) If it appears to the registrar that a company has failed to comply with any enactment requiring it— (a) to send to the registrar a document making or evidencing an alteration in the company's articles, or (b) to send to the registrar a copy of the company's articles as amended, the registrar may give notice to the company requiring it to comply."
#ASSERT `s 27(1) the registrar may give notice to the company requiring it to comply` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 27(1) the registrar may give notice to the company requiring it to comply` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 27(1) the registrar may give notice to the company requiring it to comply` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `s 27(1) the registrar may give notice to the company requiring it to comply` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE; the function is named for a power ("the registrar may give notice") and the "If it appears" gate is not closed with "only", so a failed "if" leaves the text silent (Guide, section 5, "In short"), fork F42
-- "(2) The notice must— (a) state the date on which it is issued, and (b) require the company to comply within 28 days from that date."
#ASSERT `s 27(2) the notice has the content it must have` TRUE 28 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 27(2) the notice has the content it must have` TRUE 27 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 27(2) the notice has the content it must have` TRUE 29 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 27(2) the notice has the content it must have` FALSE 28 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "(3) If the company complies with the notice within the specified time, no criminal proceedings may be brought" (notice issued 1 March 2026; 28 days later is 29 March 2026)
#ASSERT `s 27(3) criminal proceedings may be brought in respect of the failure to comply` (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE (Date 29 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 27(3) criminal proceedings may be brought in respect of the failure to comply` (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE (Date 30 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 27(3) criminal proceedings may be brought in respect of the failure to comply` (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- "(4) If the company does not comply with the notice within the specified time, it is liable to a civil penalty of £200."
#ASSERT `s 27(4) the company is liable to a civil penalty` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE (Date 29 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 27(4) the company is liable to a civil penalty` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE (Date 30 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 27(4) the company is liable to a civil penalty` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 27(4) the company is liable to a civil penalty` FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 27(4) the amount of the civil penalty, in pounds` EQUALS 200
#ASSERT `s 27(4) the civil penalty excludes liability to criminal proceedings` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "(5) The penalty may be recovered by the registrar and is to be paid into the Consolidated Fund."
#ASSERT `s 27(5) the registrar may recover the penalty` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 27(5) the registrar may recover the penalty` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 27(5) the penalty is to be paid into the Consolidated Fund` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 27(5) the penalty is to be paid into the Consolidated Fund` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the duty, run (read, not asserted). Expected, in order: FULFILLED (day 28); BREACH (day 29).
#TRACE `s 27(2) the company's duty to comply with the notice` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `s 27(2) comply with the registrar's notice` AT 28
#TRACE `s 27(2) the company's duty to comply with the notice` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `s 27(2) comply with the registrar's notice` AT 29

-- ---- s 28 ----
-- "(1) Provisions that immediately before the commencement of this Part were contained in a company's memorandum but are not provisions of the kind mentioned in section 8 ... are to be treated after the commencement of this Part as provisions of the company's articles."
#ASSERT `s 28(1) the provision is treated as a provision of the company's articles` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 28(1) the provision is treated as a provision of the company's articles` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 28(1) the provision is treated as a provision of the company's articles` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "(2) This applies not only to substantive provisions but also to provision for entrenchment"
#ASSERT `s 28(2) the treatment extends to the provision` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 28(2) the treatment extends to the provision` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 28(2) the treatment extends to the provision` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "(3) ... except that the duty under section 23(1)(a) to give notice to the registrar does not apply."
#ASSERT `s 28(3) the duty under section 23(1)(a) to give notice to the registrar applies to the provision` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 28(3) the duty under section 23(1)(a) to give notice to the registrar applies to the provision` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 29 ----
-- "(1) This Chapter applies to— (a) any special resolution; (b) any resolution or agreement agreed to by all the members of a company that, if not so agreed to, would not have been effective for its purpose unless passed as a special resolution; (c) ... class of shareholders ... (d) any resolution or agreement that effectively binds all members of a class of shareholders though not agreed to by all those members; (e) any other resolution or agreement to which this Chapter applies by virtue of any enactment."
#ASSERT `s 29(1) this Chapter applies to the resolution or agreement` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 29(1) this Chapter applies to the resolution or agreement` (JUST FALSE) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 29(1) this Chapter applies to the resolution or agreement` (JUST FALSE) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 29(1) this Chapter applies to the resolution or agreement` (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 29(1) this Chapter applies to the resolution or agreement` (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 29(1) this Chapter applies to the resolution or agreement` (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 29(1) this Chapter applies to the resolution or agreement` NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 29(1) this Chapter applies to the resolution or agreement` NOTHING TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "(2) References in subsection (1) to a member of a company ... do not include the company itself where it is such a member by virtue only of its holding shares as treasury shares."
#ASSERT `s 29(2) the member counts as a member for the purposes of subsection (1)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 29(2) the member counts as a member for the purposes of subsection (1)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 29(2) the member counts as a member for the purposes of subsection (1)` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 30 ----
-- "(1) A copy of every resolution or agreement ..., or (in the case of a resolution or agreement that is not in writing) a written memorandum setting out its terms, must be forwarded to the registrar within 15 days after it is passed or made."
#ASSERT `s 30(1) what the company must forward to the registrar` TRUE EQUALS `s 30(1) a copy of the resolution or agreement`
#ASSERT `s 30(1) what the company must forward to the registrar` FALSE EQUALS `s 30(1) a written memorandum setting out the terms of the resolution or agreement`
#ASSERT `s 30(1) the copy or memorandum was forwarded in time` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 16 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 30(1) the copy or memorandum was forwarded in time` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 17 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the duty, run (read, not asserted). Expected, in order: FULFILLED (day 15); BREACH (day 16).
#TRACE `s 30(1) the company's duty` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `s 30(1) forward the copy or memorandum to the registrar` AT 15
#TRACE `s 30(1) the company's duty` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `s 30(1) forward the copy or memorandum to the registrar` AT 16
-- "(2) If a company fails to comply with this section, an offence is committed by— (a) the company, and (b) every officer of it who is in default."
#ASSERT `s 30(2)(a) the company commits an offence` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 30(2)(a) the company commits an offence` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 30(2)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 30(2)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 30(2)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 30(2)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` FALSE NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "(3) ... a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3"
#ASSERT `s 30(3) the penalty`'s `how convicted` EQUALS `on summary conviction`
#ASSERT `s 30(3) the penalty`'s `fine not exceeding` EQUALS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1)
#ASSERT `s 30(3) the penalty`'s `daily default fine for continued contravention` EQUALS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1)
#ASSERT `s 30(3) the most the person can be fined on summary conviction, in pounds` 1000 EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT `s 30(3) the most the daily default fine can be for each day of continued contravention, in pounds` 1000 EQUALS 100
-- "(4) For the purposes of this section, a liquidator of the company is treated as an officer of it."
#ASSERT `s 30(4) the person is treated as an officer of the company for the purposes of section 30` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 30(4) the person is treated as an officer of the company for the purposes of section 30` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 31 ----
-- "(1) Unless a company's articles specifically restrict the objects of the company, its objects are unrestricted."
#ASSERT `s 31(1) the company's objects are unrestricted` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 31(1) the company's objects are unrestricted` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "(2) Where a company amends its articles so as to add, remove or alter a statement of the company's objects— (a) it must give notice to the registrar, (b) on receipt of the notice, the registrar shall register it, and (c) the amendment is not effective until entry of that notice on the register."
#ASSERT `s 31(2)(a) the company must give notice to the registrar` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 31(2)(a) the company must give notice to the registrar` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 31(2)(b) the registrar shall register the notice` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 31(2)(b) the registrar shall register the notice` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 31(2)(c) the amendment cannot yet be effective` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 31(2)(c) the amendment cannot yet be effective` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the chain, run (read, not asserted). Expected, in order: FULFILLED (company gives notice, registrar registers it); a residual obligation on the registrar alone (the company has given notice and the registrar has not yet registered it); FULFILLED (nothing amended).
#TRACE `s 31(2) the company's duty to give notice, and the registrar's duty to register it` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `s 31(2)(a) give the registrar notice of the amendment of the statement of the company's objects` AT 1
    PARTY Registrar DOES `s 31(2)(b) register the notice` AT 2
#TRACE `s 31(2) the company's duty to give notice, and the registrar's duty to register it` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `s 31(2)(a) give the registrar notice of the amendment of the statement of the company's objects` AT 1
#TRACE `s 31(2) the company's duty to give notice, and the registrar's duty to register it` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 100)
-- "(3) Any such amendment does not affect any rights or obligations of the company or render defective any legal proceedings by or against it."
#ASSERT `s 31(3) the amendment affects any rights or obligations of the company` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 31(3) the amendment affects any rights or obligations of the company` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 31(3) the amendment renders defective any legal proceedings by or against the company` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 31(3) the amendment renders defective any legal proceedings by or against the company` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "(4) In the case of a company that is a charity, the provisions of this section have effect subject to— (a) in England and Wales, sections 197 and 198 of the Charities Act 2011; (b) in Northern Ireland, section 96 of the Charities Act (Northern Ireland) 2008. (5) In the case of a company that is entered in the Scottish Charity Register, the provisions of this section have effect subject to the provisions of the Charities and Trustee Investment (Scotland) Act 2005."
#ASSERT `s 31(4) and (5) the enactments this section has effect subject to` TRUE FALSE `England and Wales` EQUALS LIST `s 31 sections 197 and 198 of the Charities Act 2011`
#ASSERT `s 31(4) and (5) the enactments this section has effect subject to` TRUE FALSE `Northern Ireland` EQUALS LIST `s 31 section 96 of the Charities Act (Northern Ireland) 2008`
#ASSERT `s 31(4) and (5) the enactments this section has effect subject to` TRUE FALSE `Scotland` EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `s 31(4) and (5) the enactments this section has effect subject to` FALSE FALSE `Northern Ireland` EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `s 31(4) and (5) the enactments this section has effect subject to` FALSE TRUE `Scotland` EQUALS LIST `s 31 the provisions of the Charities and Trustee Investment (Scotland) Act 2005`

-- ---- s 32 ----
-- "(1) A company must, on request by any member, send to him the following documents"
#ASSERT `s 32(1) the company must send the documents to the person on request` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 32(1) the company must send the documents to the person on request` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 32(1) the company must send the documents to the person on request` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
